_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "No abrupt partner turnover. Group-level neighbourhood-change series are flat-to-decaying at bandwidths 2500/5000/10000 with no isolated spike, and the 5000-unit before/after sets overlap heavily (26 shared contacts, J~0.52). Edge-level snapshot diffs give jaccard 0.00-0.21, but this is because group members rotate duty (719/836 -> 1224 -> 1318/1374 -> 1598/1610) while contacting an identical ~30-node external core, confirmed by direct neighbour listings for 103, 1224, 1374 and 1610 in four disjoint sub-windows. Activity is stationary with no bursts and degrees are uniform across members, ruling out volume or onset/offset explanations."}, "raw_final_response": "**Conclusion:** The apparent \"regime switch\" is an artifact of *which group member* is active, not of *whom the group talks to*.\n\nKey findings:\n- Group-level turnover (step_02, step_06, step_10) never shows a localized spike against a flat baseline: at bandwidth 5000 the series wanders between 0.23 and 0.44 with a shallow \"peak\" at 35294 that is barely above its neighbours, and the before/after contact lists share 26 of ~50 union members (J\u22480.52). At bandwidth 10000 the curve is monotonically *decaying* (0.55\u21920.45), i.e. background drift, not a step.\n- Edge-level diffs look dramatic (J=0.21 at 35294, J=0.00 at 40166 and between the first/last 5000-unit slices), but the removed/added samples reveal the cause: `719,836\u2192*` is replaced by `1224\u2192*`, then `866,1224\u2192*` by `1318,1374\u2192*`, then `103,462\u2192*` by `1598,1610\u2192*` \u2014 always **the same external partner set**.\n- Direct verification: node 103 in [25166,30165] (step_11), 1224 in [35294,40294] (step_14), 1374 in [40166,45165] (step_13) and 1610 in [50167,55166] (step_12) all contact the identical ~30-node core {57,156,234,235,255,324,354,402,535,559,617,641,728,756,874,931,1010,1133,1141,1182,1312,1357,1416,1422,1436,1538,1656,1779,1838,1893}. The old contacts never give way to new ones.\n- Confounder controls: volume is essentially stationary (~56\u00b117 per bin, step_03) with **zero** bursts at z\u22651.5 (step_09), and every group member has near-identical degree (92\u201397 events, 31\u201336 partners; step_07), so no member-specific onset/offset either.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_459f9d4b\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [103, 462, 719, 836, 866, 1224, 1318, 1374, 1415, 1598, 1610, 1826],\n  \"window\": [25166, 55166],\n  \"confidence\": 0.83,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"No abrupt partner turnover. Group-level neighbourhood-change series are flat-to-decaying at bandwidths 2500/5000/10000 with no isolated spike, and the 5000-unit before/after sets overlap heavily (26 shared contacts, J~0.52). Edge-level snapshot diffs give jaccard 0.00-0.21, but this is because group members rotate duty (719/836 -> 1224 -> 1318/1374 -> 1598/1610) while contacting an identical ~30-node external core, confirmed by direct neighbour listings for 103, 1224, 1374 and 1610 in four disjoint sub-windows. Activity is stationary with no bursts and degrees are uniform across members, ruling out volume or onset/offset explanations.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 56207, "total_output_tokens": 6066, "total_tokens": 62273, "total_latency_ms": 84209, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}